tor for BBB-crossing, supporting translation to humans.Available for large-scale manufacturing, ensuring clinical comparability and predictability.View PresentationBrainDyno-ahqLaunched in 2025, the Dyno-ahq capsid is optimized for widespread IV delivery to the brain, with exceptional liver detargeting and a highly conserved mechanism for blood-brain barrier crossing.Launched in 2025, the Dyno-ahq capsid is optimized for widespread IV delivery to the brain, with exceptional liver detargeting and a highly conserved mechanism for blood-brain barrier crossing.Expand ImageCrosses BBB reaching up to 30% of NHP neurons at a dose of 3e13 vg/kg, with 280x higher brain transduction vs AAV9.50x lower liver transduction compared to AAV9.Intravenous injection enables more uniform brain transduction and broader patient access.Optimized and validated in NHPs.Highly conserved candidate receptor for BBB-crossing supports translation to humans.View PresentationBrainDyno-hc9Launched in 2023, the Dyno-hc9 capsid (aka bCap 1) was the first Dyno capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery across the blood-brain barrier, with broad CNS tropism and liver detargeting.Launched in 2023, the Dyno-hc9 capsid (aka bCap 1) was the first Dyno capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery across the blood-brain barrier, with broad CNS tropism and liver detargeting.Expand Image100x higher brain transduction and 10x lower liver transduction vs. AAV9, with similar production efficiency.Transduces neurons and glia, including cell-types relevant for ALS, Huntington’s, Parkinson’s Disease.Reaches deep brain regions and the spinal cord.Easy intravenous injection enables uniform transduction and broad patient access.Optimized and validated in NHPs.View PresentationMuscle/NeuromuscularDyno-bn8Launched in 2025, the Dyno-bn8 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal and cardiac muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle and neuromuscular gene therapies.Launched in 2025, the Dyno-bn8 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal and cardiac muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle and neuromuscular gene therapies.Expand ImageEven at the low dose of 5e12 vg/kg (25x lower dose than Elevidys), transduces 73-88% of myofibers in NHP skeletal muscles.Safe and broad muscle delivery, due to low dose and low biodistribution to liver and spleen.Transduces 35-42% of NHP cardiac cells at 1.6e13 vg/kg.Confidence in human translation given highly conserved entry receptor and in vitro transduction of human muscle cell lines.Easily manufactured at a large scale and compatible with existing AAV9-based processes.View PresentationMuscle/NeuromuscularDyno-n96Launched at ASGCT 2026, the Dyno-n96 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle gene therapies.Launched at ASGCT 2026, the Dyno-n96 capsid enables therapeutic delivery to skeletal muscles at IV doses as low as 5e12 vg/kg, dramatically improving safety for muscle gene therapies.Expand ImageAAVrh74-based, with stronger muscle transduction compared to other natural AAV serotypes.Even at the low dose of 5e12 vg/kg (25x lower dose than Elevidys), transduces 74% of myofibers in NHP skeletal muscles.Safe and broad muscle delivery, due to low dose and low biodistribution to liver (1.4x < AAVrh74).Confidence in human translation given in vitro transduction of human muscle cell lines.Easily manufactured at a large scale and compatible with existing AAV9-based processes.View PresentationMuscle/NeuromuscularDyno-3hvLaunched in 2025, Dyno-3hv is the first capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery to the multiple tissues affected by neuromuscular disorders, including the heart, skeletal muscle and CNS.Launched in 2025, Dyno-3hv is the first capsid optimized for highly efficient delivery to the multiple tissues affected by neuromuscular disorders, including the heart, skeletal muscle and CNS.Expand ImageTransduces 50-90% of myofibers in NHP skeletal muscles, and multiple regions of the heart and CNS at doses as low as 4e12 vg/kg.Low biodistribution to off-target peripheral organs, with liver biodistribution <10 vg/dg and spleen <0.5 vg/dg at a dose of 4e12 vg/kg, supporting safer IV dosing.Intravenous injection enables more uniform transduction across cells and tissues and broader patient access.Confidence in human translation given highly conserved entry receptor and in vitro transduction of human muscle cell lines.Easily manufactured at large scales and compatible with AAV9-based processes.View PresentationEyeDyno-4z2Launched in 2025, Dyno-4z2 capsid is optimized for highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with field-leading targeting of bipolar cells in the inner nuclear layer.Launched in 2025, Dyno-4z2 capsid is optimized for highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with field-leading targeting of bipolar cells in the inner nuclear layer.Expand Image>40x retinal transduction vs AAV2, outperforms all tested externally engineered capsids at doses of 1e10-1e11 vg/eye.An ideal capsid for optogenetic gene therapies: 5x transduction of bipolar cells in the inner nuclear layer compared to a reference externally engineered capsid.Intravitreal injection enables easy administration and broad patient access.Optimized and validated in NHPs and mice, supporting translation to humans.Easily manufactured at large scales and compatible with AAV2-based processes.View PresentationEyeDyno-86mLaunched in 2023, the Dyno-86m vector was the first Dyno ocular capsid optimized for easy and highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with a broad retinal tropism.Launched in 2023, the Dyno-86m vector was the first Dyno ocular capsid optimized for easy and highly efficient delivery to the retina through intravitreal injection, with a broad retinal tropism.Expand Image80x higher retinal transduction vs AAV2, with similar production efficiency.Transduces retinal ganglion cells, bipolar cells and rod photoreceptors.Reaches macula and peripheral retina, enabling biofactory, neuroprotective, optogenetic and photoreceptor therapies.Easy intravitreal injection enables broad patient access.Optimized and validated in NHPs.View PresentationStart collaborating with DynoReach out to partnerwith@dynotx.com to learn how Dyno’s capsid platform can level-up your gene therapies.343 Arsenal StWatertown, MA 02472Gene DeliveryPartnershipsApproachAboutNewsBlogCareersFrontiers NetworkGATC 2026© Dyno 2026Privacy PolicyTerms + ConditionsDyno Therapeutics, DYNO, the DYNO logo, and mountain design are registered trademarks of Dyno Therapeutics, Inc. All rights reserved."
